 dance numbers KC  undercover instead had dangerous stunts  fight choreography rehearsals and  training but there's even more that can  go into just one day of shooting the spy  series a typical day for any film or  television show can be as long as 12  hours per day ranging to as high as 16  to 18 hours for the cast of KC  Undercover their long day starts with a  table read where the entire cast sits  around a very large table and does a  read-through of the whole episode once  that is complete they then go into  rehearsals for each scene on set from  there the actors complete sometimes  several hours in hair and makeup and  wardrobe  once they physically transform into the  KC characters we know and love they head  back to  and that's where the magic finally  happens the cameras start rolling and  they start shooting the show to create  television magic it's a lot of work an  effort to create just one 30-minute  episode being a spy means going on lots  of undercover missions and for every  mission you've always got to dress the  part in disguise of course for the cast  of case the undercover that means lots  and lots of wardrobe changes from punk  rocker to disco diva to an old woman and  even a cowgirl every episode zendaya  goes through a huge range of fun and  very wacky costumes the actors have even  shared an inside look behind the scenes  to show off their characters looks  although regular teenage KC has a simple  wardrobe normally wearing jeans a  t-shirt and some sneaker wedges paired  with her usual plaid shirt wrapped  around her waist her alter-ego Casey the  spy has lots of fun being in her spy  disguises according to the Disney  Channel itself the hour-long episode  entitled tightrope of doom took Sandhya  approximately 11 hours to transform into  four characters in the circus episode in  fact there were nearly 100 costumes  featured in that one episode wowza  that's a lot my style is perpetually  cutting a breeze did you ever wonder  what Casey actually stands for turns out  it's Katrina Charlotte although it's  never actually spoken in any episode  according to several fan pages such as  fandom comm that is Casey's real name we  can confirm that in season 1 episode 7  however Casey's father Craig actually  refers to her as KC Coretta Scott King  Cooper turns out her middle name is a  tribute to the late Coretta Scott King  Martin Luther King Jr's wife and a  leader in the civil rights movement from  the 1960s a very fitting name for a show  that zendaya thought to be diverse with  an all-black family we think mrs. King  would be proud okay I don't know what is  wrong with you people  but if you think my parents are gonna  pay some big ransom you are sadly  mistaken  zendaya has admitted in an article with  variety that she grew up watching that  so Raven another classic Disney show  from 2003 she revealed that she learned  a lot of her comedy from Raven and her  show  turns out the executives of KC  undercover were also the creators of  that So Raven and knew that zendaya was  a huge fan at the former Disney Channel  star she considered Raven her idol not  only as a performer but as a person so  when Disney reached out to Raven to be a  part of the show they knew how much that  would mean to zendaya executive producer  Rob Lauder Stein called it his gift to  the lead actress Raven came on for a  two-part episode and producer said the  actresses performances were like a  classic buddy comedy most memorably when  they dressed up as old janitors for a  scene in the episode Sunday I confessed  that Ravens presence on set pushed her  to step up her acting game and really  get creative with her performance  knowing she based her comedy off of the  veteran Disney actress she said it made  her try new things and really discover  herself in the process did you know that  zendaya is one of a handful of Disney  stars who have acted in more than one  Disney show the actress is known for her  lead role as KC Cooper but in